Here we can collect successful builds for various clusters and machines. These
recipes are mostly for own reference but can of course serve as first steps
for users trying to install DIRAC on similar machines.

 Don't forget to run pamadm first !

stallo (x86_64 linux cluster) 2011-02-20
----------------------------------------
$ module load intel-compiler/11.1 openmpi/1.4 mkl/10.2.0.013 cmake
$ ./setup --fc=mpif90 --cc=mpicc --mpi --math="-L/global/apps/intel/mkl/10.2.0.013/lib/em64t -lmkl_lapack -lmkl_intel_lp64 -lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core -lguide -lpthread"
$ cd cbuild
$ make
$ cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/global/apps/dirac/latest ..
$ make install

titan (x86_64 linux cluster) 2011-02-20
---------------------------------------
$ module load intel/11.1 openmpi/1.4.3.intel cmake/2.6.4
$ ./setup --fc=mpif90 --cc=mpicc --mpi --math="-L/site/Goto-library/AuthenticAMD-x86_64/ifort/ -lblas -L/site/Goto-library/AuthenticAMD-x86_64/ifort/ -llapack"
$ cd cbuild
$ make
$ cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/home/bast/bin/dirac ..
$ make install

larry (i686 laptop running ubuntu) 2011-02-20
---------------------------------------------
$ ./setup --fc=ifort --cc=icc --math="-L/opt/intel/mkl/10.2.6.038/lib/32 -lmkl_lapack -lmkl_intel -lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core -lguide -lpthread"
$ cd cbuild
$ make
$ cd ..
$ ln -s cbuild/dirac.x

thor (laptop running suse; cmake 2.8.3) 2011-02-20
--------------------------------------------------
$ ./setup --fc=gfortran --cc=gcc --math="-L/opt/intel/mkl/10.0.1.014/lib/32 -lmkl_lapack -lmkl_intel -lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core -lguide -lpthread" --prefix="/home/stefan/prog/dirac/seriell/mytrunk/build_gfort_seq"
$ cd build_gfort_seq
$ make
$ cd ..
$ ln -s build_gfort_seq/dirac.x

ilias@frpd2.utcpd.sk (Lunix x86_64) 2011-02-21
------------------------------------------------------
$ ./setup --fc=g95 --cc=gcc-4.2 --int64 --nomath
$ ln -sf  cbuild/dirac.x dirac.x
$ cd cbuild
$ cmake ..
$ make

ilias@miro.pd.uniza.sk (Lunix x86_64) 2011-03-08
------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ ./pamadm -a --xcfun
$ ./setup --fc=mpi90 --cc=mpicc --cpp=mpiCC --int64 --nomath --mpi --runtest_mpi=2 --debug
$ ln -sf  cbuild/dirac.x .
$ cd cbuild
$ make -j 2

